#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/repetition-codes/extracted-outputs/67acea4f-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/repetition-codes/extracted-outputs/67acea4f-0.avif)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Paso 3. Ejecutar usando primitivas de Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Paso 4: Post-procesar y devolver el resultado en el formato clásico deseado {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will now compare the error rates vs. time between the logical memory using the 3-qubit repetition code on the one hand, and the individual unencoded reference qubits on the other hand.\n"
msgstr "Ahora compararemos las tasas de error frente al tiempo entre la memoria lógica usando el código de repetición de 3 qubits por un lado, y los qubits de referencia individuales sin codificar por otro lado.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/repetition-codes/extracted-outputs/72ad282b-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/repetition-codes/extracted-outputs/72ad282b-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We clearly see an improved lifetime of the $|\\bar{1}\\rangle$ state, even compared to the best (unencoded) physical qubits. However, keep in mind that this experiment just corrects one type of error, namely bit-flips. Can you improve the lifetime of the logical qubit? You might want to explore optimizing the delay time, scaling up the size of the repetition code beyond $n=3$, etc.\n"
msgstr "Vemos claramente un tiempo de vida mejorado del estado $|\\bar{1}\\rangle$, incluso en comparación con los mejores qubits físicos (sin codificar). Sin embargo, ten en cuenta que este experimento solo corrige un tipo de error, a saber, bit-flips. ¿Puedes mejorar el tiempo de vida del qubit lógico? Podrías explorar la optimización del tiempo de retraso, escalar el tamaño del código de repetición más allá de $n=3$, etc.\n"

